<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto V, Margrave of Brandenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1246–1298</span> · Also known as Otto the Long</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto V, called the Long, was a margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> of the Ascanian house. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a> was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-marchfeld">Battle on the Marchfeld</a> in 1278, he became guardian of the young Wenceslaus II and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. His regency, during which Brandenburg troops occupied the country and the boy king was held away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, was remembered as a time of disorder.</p></div>
